From: WinRE (vendored patch for x64dbg-MCP-Server, upstream commit snapshot 2026-08)
Subject: [PATCH] setHardwareBreakpoint: report cmdExec failure as an error

Upstream returned fmtResult("Failed to set hardware breakpoint.") with
is_error=false, so MCP callers saw ok:true while nothing was registered.
Our OEP tracing depends on knowing the BP actually landed, so failures
must surface as errors (fmtErr).

Apply to: src/mcp/tools.zig  (fn setHardwareBreakpoint)

--- a/src/mcp/tools.zig
+++ b/src/mcp/tools.zig
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
-    return fmtResult(out, "{s}", .{if (ok) "Hardware breakpoint set." else "Failed to set hardware breakpoint"});
+    // NOTE (WinRE): report cmdExec failure as an error, not success text.
+    // Previously fmtResult hid failures ("Failed to..." with is_error=false),
+    // so callers saw ok:true with nothing registered.
+    if (!ok) return fmtErr(out, "Failed to set hardware breakpoint.", .{});
+    return fmtResult(out, "{s}", .{"Hardware breakpoint set."});

NOTE: the MCP plugin ships in the vendored x64dbg-MCP project (MIT), not in
the WinRE repo - see docs/X64DBG-MCP.md for the source + build steps.
